Real captcha solving + honest sent/failed verdicts

THE PROVEN BUG CHAIN
  1. detect_captcha() was a bare substring match ("hcaptcha" in html). Measured
     against a real browser: 1,429 pages were tagged as captcha when NO WIDGET
     EVER LOADED -- the word only appeared in a JS template string. Shopify
     contact pages are full of this: window.hcaptcha is undefined, no widget
     script. Those pages were then filed needs_manual UNCONDITIONALLY by the
     hard_captcha branch, guaranteeing an unconfirmable verdict at scale.
  2. The browser tier never clicked or solved a captcha. It clicked Submit, a
     puzzle appeared, it moved on. Watched live by the user.
  3. _verdict() grepped the page for thank|success|sent and called that
     "submitted". Static page copy contains those words, so an unsolved puzzle
     was logged as a success. That is why ~5 confirmation emails came from
     hundreds of "sends".

FIXES
  core/solver.py (NEW)
    NoneCap wired in -- the API key the user had already paid for and that no
    code referenced. POST /v1/solves?wait=90 -> P1_ token; GET /v1/solves/{id}
    to poll; GET /v1/me for balance. Token injected into h-captcha-response /
    g-recaptcha-response.
    Type is corrected FROM THE KEY FORMAT because selectors lie: "6LdNfLIZ..."
    is a Google key, UUIDs are hCaptcha. graff.com was mislabelled hcaptcha and
    got a 422 until this was fixed.
    VERIFIED LIVE: real P1_ token, 2508 chars, 13.0s.

  core/submitter_browser.py
    _detect_widget() -- reads the LIVE widget and its real sitekey, requires an
    actual element, and forces kind from key format.
    _verdict() -- evidence hierarchy: success URL > success wording AND form
    gone > explicit captcha/error notice AND form present (needs_manual) >
    success wording alone > nothing. A puzzle that was never solved now reports
    needs_manual instead of a fake success.
    Watchdog: browser_site_budget + browser_nav_timeout. rumanoffs.com wedged
    the whole run for 23 minutes because nothing bounded a site.
    --show-browser / --slow-mo so the user can watch it work.

  core/submitter_http.py
    detect_captcha() now requires real widget evidence (element+sitekey, or the
    loader script, or the challenges endpoint). reCAPTCHA is checked BEFORE
    hCaptcha because a page can mention hcaptcha without using it.
    needs_manual now says "interactive captcha, no token (needs browser/solver)"
    so the browser tier is clearly the answer rather than lumping it with every
    ambiguous 2xx.

KNOWN LIMITS, stated honestly
  * NoneCap supports only hcaptcha, hcaptcha_enterprise, recaptcha_v3.
    There is NO recaptcha_v2 type, and recaptcha_v3 currently returns
    "maintenance". So Google-key widgets cannot be API-solved yet; the browser
    clicks them and often self-solves.
  * v3 is invisible and ByteDance-check only on submit, so it legitimately
    reads as "no widget" pre-submit.

MEASURED RESULT of the browser tier before these fixes: 101 submitted,
0 needs_manual on the apify batch, vs 7% confirmed on the http tier.
